---
// Week 4 "See It": a potentiometer used two ways inside a guitar — as a
// volume control (a variable voltage divider to ground) and as a tone
// control (a variable resistor in series with a fixed capacitor to ground,
// forming an adjustable RC low-pass). Simplified sketches, not accurate
// schematics — the wiper's drawn travel is illustrative, matching
// CLAUDE.md's "avoid unnecessary circuit-analysis detail."
---

<div class="pot-diagrams">
  <figure class="pot-card bench-module">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 160 90" role="img" aria-label="Volume control: a potentiometer wired as a voltage divider, with the wiper tapping off a fraction of the signal to send onward and the rest sent to ground.">
      <line x1="10" y1="20" x2="60" y2="20" class="wire" />
      <rect x="60" y="12" width="40" height="16" class="pot-track" />
      <line x1="100" y1="20" x2="130" y2="20" class="wire" />
      <path d="M 62 26 L 130 26 M 62 34 L 130 34 M 62 42 L 130 42" class="ground" />
      <line x1="80" y1="12" x2="80" y2="46" class="wiper" />
      <path d="M 74 46 L 80 40 L 86 46" class="wiper-arrow" fill="none" />
      <line x1="80" y1="46" x2="130" y2="46" class="wire" />
      <circle cx="10" cy="20" r="2.5" class="node" />
      <circle cx="130" cy="20" r="2.5" class="node" />
      <circle cx="130" cy="46" r="2.5" class="node" />
      <text x="130" y="16" class="part-label">in</text>
      <text x="134" y="24" class="part-label">out</text>
      <text x="134" y="50" class="part-label">to ground</text>
    </svg>
    <figcaption>
      <span class="pot-label">Volume control</span>
      <span class="pot-description">The wiper taps a fraction of the input signal and sends the rest to ground — turning the pot down sends proportionally more of the signal to ground instead of onward.</span>
    </figcaption>
  </figure>

  <figure class="pot-card bench-module">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 160 90" role="img" aria-label="Tone control: a potentiometer used as a variable resistor in series with a fixed capacitor to ground, forming a low-pass filter whose cutoff frequency the wiper adjusts.">
      <line x1="10" y1="20" x2="55" y2="20" class="wire" />
      <rect x="55" y="12" width="40" height="16" class="pot-track" />
      <line x1="75" y1="12" x2="75" y2="4" class="wiper" />
      <path d="M 69 4 L 75 -2 L 81 4" class="wiper-arrow" fill="none" transform="translate(0,6)" />
      <line x1="95" y1="20" x2="120" y2="20" class="wire" />
      <line x1="120" y1="20" x2="120" y2="40" class="wire" />
      <line x1="108" y1="46" x2="132" y2="46" class="cap-plate" />
      <line x1="108" y1="52" x2="132" y2="52" class="cap-plate" />
      <line x1="120" y1="40" x2="120" y2="46" class="wire" />
      <path d="M 112 58 L 128 58 M 112 64 L 128 64 M 112 70 L 128 70" class="ground" />
      <line x1="120" y1="52" x2="120" y2="58" class="wire" />
      <circle cx="10" cy="20" r="2.5" class="node" />
      <text x="6" y="14" class="part-label">in</text>
      <text x="122" y="50" class="part-label">C</text>
      <text x="70" y="8" class="part-label">wiper sets R</text>
    </svg>
    <figcaption>
      <span class="pot-label">Tone control</span>
      <span class="pot-description">The wiper sets the effective resistance in series with a fixed capacitor to ground — together an RC low-pass whose cutoff, f_c = 1/(2πRC), the wiper sweeps.</span>
    </figcaption>
  </figure>
</div>

<style>
  .pot-diagrams {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(15rem, 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .pot-card {
    margin: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }

  .pot-card svg {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    display: block;
    overflow: visible;
  }

  .wire {
    stroke: var(--at-text-secondary);
    stroke-width: 1.5;
    fill: none;
  }

  .pot-track {
    fill: var(--at-bg);
    stroke: var(--at-accent);
    stroke-width: 1.5;
  }

  .wiper {
    stroke: var(--bench-phosphor, var(--at-accent));
    stroke-width: 1.5;
  }

  .wiper-arrow {
    stroke: var(--bench-phosphor, var(--at-accent));
    stroke-width: 1.5;
  }

  .ground {
    stroke: var(--at-text-secondary);
    stroke-width: 1.5;
    fill: none;
  }

  .cap-plate {
    stroke: var(--at-text-secondary);
    stroke-width: 2;
  }

  .node {
    fill: var(--at-text-secondary);
  }

  .part-label {
    font-family: var(--bench-readout, var(--at-font-mono));
    font-size: 6px;
    fill: var(--at-text-secondary);
  }

  figcaption {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.15rem;
  }

  .pot-label {
    font-family: var(--bench-readout, var(--at-font-mono));
    font-size: var(--at-font-size-sm);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.03em;
    color: var(--at-text);
  }

  .pot-description {
    font-size: var(--at-font-size-xs);
    color: var(--at-text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.35;
  }
</style>
